WEBVTT

NOTE Internet Monitor tour: overview (en). Generated by tools/tutorial/build.cjs.

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:03.124
This is the Overview,
the first page you see.

2
00:00:03.124 --> 00:00:07.767
It shows how your internet is doing right now,
and what happened recently.

3
00:00:08.167 --> 00:00:10.925
The big card at the top is the live status.

4
00:00:10.925 --> 00:00:14.067
Green and Connected means
every check is passing.

5
00:00:14.067 --> 00:00:18.493
Orange means Unstable: the line works,
but it is slow or losing data.

6
00:00:18.493 --> 00:00:19.968
Red means Disconnected.

7
00:00:19.968 --> 00:00:23.752
The line under it says in plain
words where the problem is,

8
00:00:23.752 --> 00:00:26.767
for example at your router
or at your provider.

9
00:00:27.167 --> 00:00:30.085
On the right you see how long
it has been in this state,

10
00:00:30.085 --> 00:00:32.900
when the last check ran,
and how often the app checks.

11
00:00:33.300 --> 00:00:36.547
These four tiles are the
numbers behind the status.

12
00:00:36.547 --> 00:00:41.257
Response time is how long a reply takes,
in milliseconds. Lower is better.

13
00:00:41.257 --> 00:00:44.249
Fluctuation is how much
that time jumps around.

14
00:00:44.249 --> 00:00:47.559
Data loss is the share of
checks that got no answer.

15
00:00:47.559 --> 00:00:51.633
Uptime is the share of checks that
passed since the app started.

16
00:00:52.033 --> 00:00:55.700
The outage timeline shows the
last 24 hours as one bar.

17
00:00:55.700 --> 00:00:59.967
Green is connected, orange is unstable,
and red is disconnected.

18
00:00:59.967 --> 00:01:04.500
Striped grey means the app was not
running, so nothing was measured.

19
00:01:04.500 --> 00:01:07.100
Switch to 7 days to see the whole week.

20
00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:10.961
Point at any red or orange
part of the bar to see exactly

21
00:01:10.961 --> 00:01:14.300
when it started, when it ended,
and how long it lasted.

22
00:01:14.700 --> 00:01:19.325
What your data says reads the last 30
days for you and points out what matters.

23
00:01:19.325 --> 00:01:22.369
Each tip explains what it
means and what to do next,

24
00:01:22.369 --> 00:01:26.233
like opening a complaint when the
fault is on the provider's side.

25
00:01:26.633 --> 00:01:29.933
The router card reads your
router on your home network.

26
00:01:29.933 --> 00:01:32.933
Line to the provider shows
whether the line is up.

27
00:01:32.933 --> 00:01:38.033
The text under the figures says how it's read:
the router's own page, on this Huawei.

28
00:01:38.033 --> 00:01:42.833
If your router isn't supported yet,
it says so, with a button to help us add it.

29
00:01:43.233 --> 00:01:48.290
Noise margin, or SNR, shows how clean the line is.
Higher is better.

30
00:01:48.290 --> 00:01:54.313
Below about 6 dB, a DSL line drops easily,
and that is the provider's job to fix.

31
00:01:54.313 --> 00:01:58.700
Attenuation is how much the
signal fades on its way to you.

32
00:01:59.100 --> 00:02:03.219
Below that you see how much data
you used since your plan renewed.

33
00:02:03.219 --> 00:02:07.900
Set your plan's data limit, and the app
warns you at 80 and at 100 percent.

34
00:02:08.300 --> 00:02:11.572
The response time chart shows
the last checks one by one.

35
00:02:11.572 --> 00:02:14.326
A line that stays low and
flat is what you want.

36
00:02:14.326 --> 00:02:16.967
Tall spikes mean the
connection is struggling.

37
00:02:17.367 --> 00:02:20.766
Recent events lists every
change since the app started:

38
00:02:20.766 --> 00:02:24.722
when the connection dropped,
what failed, and when it came back.

39
00:02:24.722 --> 00:02:26.700
View history opens the full log.

40
00:02:27.100 --> 00:02:30.792
Availability shows how much
of the time your internet

41
00:02:30.792 --> 00:02:34.833
worked today, in the last 7 days,
and in the last 30 days.

42
00:02:35.233 --> 00:02:38.019
Check targets lists the
servers the app tests

43
00:02:38.019 --> 00:02:41.052
every few seconds,
and whether each one answered.

44
00:02:41.052 --> 00:02:43.033
You can change them in Settings.

45
00:02:43.433 --> 00:02:48.450
The status pill at the top stays on every page,
and the bell holds your latest alerts.

46
00:02:48.450 --> 00:02:51.367
The number on it counts
the ones you haven't seen.

47
00:02:51.767 --> 00:02:55.469
Every page has a How this page
works button like this one.

48
00:02:55.469 --> 00:02:59.300
It opens a short video about that page.
Thanks for watching!
